<h2>How the calculation works</h2><p>Goods cost = units × product cost per unit. Shipment charges are freight, duty, non-recoverable taxes and other entered costs. Total landed cost is goods cost plus shipment charges, and landed cost per unit divides that total by the number of units.</p><h2>How to use the result</h2><p>Use landed cost rather than supplier price alone when setting marketplace prices, planning reorder quantities or comparing sourcing options. It makes shipment-level costs visible at the unit level.</p><h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2><p>Actual import duty and tax treatment depends on product classification, origin, destination and business tax status. Recoverable credits should generally not be treated as permanent cost. This calculator does not determine customs classification or tax liability.</p><h2>Example</h2><p>Changing shipment size can materially change per-unit landed cost because fixed freight and handling costs are spread across more or fewer units.</p>
